    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add Safari notes documenting a known IME composition bug: the <code class=\"notranslate\">keydown</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">input</code> events for the key that completes an IME composition session are dispatched <em>after</em> the <code class=\"notranslate\">compositionend</code> event, so their <code class=\"notranslate\">isComposing</code> value is incorrectly <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code>. Notes are added to:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.KeyboardEvent.isComposing</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.InputEvent.isComposing</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Support values are left unchanged, since the bug does not warrant marking these features as partial or unsupported. The notes are scoped to the <code class=\"notranslate\">isComposing</code> properties only, since that is the observable symptom; the <code class=\"notranslate\">keydown</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">input</code> events themselves are correctly supported.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The bug is still reproducible in Safari 26.3 on macOS. A fix (<a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/311717\" rel=\"nofollow\">bug 311717</a>) is implemented behind the <code class=\"notranslate\">InputMethodUsesCorrectKeyEventOrder</code> preference, which is still marked as unstable.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/165004\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/b/165004</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/311717\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/b/311717</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29998.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4829229099\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29998\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29998/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29998\">#29998</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30009",
            "title": "Note Safari IME key event ordering bug affecting isComposing",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-08T13:23:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-08T13:08:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a <code class=\"notranslate\">subfeature_outside_parent_range</code> check to the <code class=\"notranslate\">Consistency</code> linter that flags a sub-feature declaring current or <code class=\"notranslate\">preview</code> support under the canonical feature name while the parent's canonical-name support exists but is no longer current (entirely <code class=\"notranslate\">version_removed</code>, or only available behind a flag). Prefixed and alternative-name statements are intentionally ignored, since BCD does not consistently propagate those to sub-features.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This catches inconsistencies the scalar <code class=\"notranslate\">version_added</code> checks miss — such as a child in <code class=\"notranslate\">preview</code> under a parent whose only unprefixed support was removed (the case from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4724227480\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29904\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29904/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29904\">#29904</a> that motivated the issue).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also fixes the 24 pre-existing data inconsistencies the new check surfaces:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.GeolocationCoordinates</code> [opera]: drop the stray <code class=\"notranslate\">Coordinates</code> alternative name so the parent matches <code class=\"notranslate\">opera_android</code> and its own members.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.builtins.Temporal</code> [safari]: drop the stale <code class=\"notranslate\">useTemporal</code> flag; the namespace is exposed unflagged in preview alongside its members.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.WebTransport</code> parameter sub-features [deno]: add the <code class=\"notranslate\">--unstable-net</code> flag carried by the interface and its methods.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.Navigator.activeVRDisplays.secure_context_required</code> [firefox]: track the parent's removal at 98 and flag-gated support thereafter.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">css.properties.resize</code> values [firefox_android]: replace <code class=\"notranslate\">mirror</code> with the parent's \"recognized, but has no effect\" removal at 79.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added 14 unit tests in <code class=\"notranslate\">lint/linter/test-consistency.test.js</code> (positive cases incl. the issue's own example, plus negative guards for <code class=\"notranslate\">≤</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">true</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">mirror</code>/prefixed/flagged children).</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npm test</code> passes; <code class=\"notranslate\">npm run lint -- --fail-on-warnings</code> passes with zero findings across the dataset.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29958.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4785560237\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29958\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29958/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29958\">#29958</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30002",
            "title": "Lint that a child feature's version range is inside its parent's range",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-08T10:26:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-08T10:25:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update Chromium to full support for WebGPU in version 144+. No more partial as it now also ships on Linux. The remark that Linux support is Intel Gen12+ GPUs only, is mentioned in a note still but without partial_implementation: true.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Linux support enabled in <a href=\"https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/0e492e6f38a84951f18d3cb3168b8ed091862738\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/0e492e6f38a84951f18d3cb3168b8ed091862738</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-144#webgpu_on_linux\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-144#webgpu_on_linux</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28451.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3622558757\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28451\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28451/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28451\">#28451</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2252751022\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/915\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/915/hovercard?comment_id=4851590415&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/915#issuecomment-4851590415\">web-platform-dx/web-features#915 (comment)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3231699289\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/202\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/202/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/202\">web-platform-dx/developer-signals#202</a></li>\n</ul>",
